<li><a name="n2" id="n2"></a>From 1 Peter 4:7, New Revised Standard Bible.</li>
<li><a name="n3" id="n3"></a>See &ldquo;Edward Gibbon,&rdquo; National Review, January 1856, 1&ndash;32.</li>
<li><a name="n4" id="n4"></a>Title XI of the Dodd&shy;&ndash;Frank Wall Street Reform and  Consumer Protection Act has since amended the Federal Reserve Act to restrict  13(3) emergency lending to programs with prior approval of the Secretary of the  Treasury and designed to provide liquidity to the financial system, not an  individual entity or insolvent firm(s).</li>
<li><a name="n5" id="n5"></a>See Churchill,  by Paul Johnson, New York: Penguin Group, 2009, pp. 52&ndash;54.</li>
<li><a name="n6" id="n6"></a>&ldquo;Recession Over, Dallas Fed Chief Says, but Jobs  Lag,&rdquo; by Brendan Case, Dallas Morning  News, Aug. 26, 2009.</li>
<li><a name="n7" id="n7"></a>&ldquo;Storms on the Horizon,&rdquo; speech by Richard W. Fisher,  May 28, 2008, www.dallasfed.org/news/speeches/fisher/2008/fs080528.cfm.</li>
<li><a name="n8" id="n8"></a>See &ldquo;The Liquidation of Government Debt,&rdquo; by Carmen  M. Reinhart and M. Belen Sbrancia, NBER Working Paper no. 16893, National  Bureau of Economic Research, March 2011.</li>
<li><a name="n9" id="n9"></a>Lone Star: A  History of Texas and the Texans, by  T.R. Fehrenbach, New York: Macmillan Publishing Co., 1985, p. 717.</li>
